From: weizxfree <weizhangxiang2022@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:40:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(mcp): let an external agent edit the open documents
 like the built-in one

- MCP commands reach the documents open in browser tabs, which join
  open_documents (and can be closed from the server)
- list_docx_tools / run_docx_tool run the editor's own document tools with
  the in-app executor and stores; `track: true` records the edit as a
  revision whatever the document's setting; `author` names the revisions'
  and comments' author
- list_xlsx_tools / run_xlsx_tool do the same for an open workbook with the
  spreadsheet assistant's tools, its base prompt coming along as the guide;
  worksheets may be named wherever a tool takes an id
- slide_ops_guide gives apply_slide_ops callers the op reference the
  in-app slides assistant loads
- save_checkpoint / restore_checkpoint: whole-document rollback points
- export_document converts in the running app, one at a time
The agent commands live in mcp-agent-commands.ts (docs, sheets),
docx-/xlsx-agent-tools.ts and slides-guide-tools.ts; the upstream files
carry one routing or spread line each.
